# Error Handling & Security

## Error Handling
- All HTTP errors flow through Axios interceptor in `QueryProvider.tsx`
- UI components rarely call `toast` directly
- Use debounced toasts for repeated errors: `debounce(toast.error, 250)`
- For 422 validation errors, reuse `use422FormErrorSetter` helper
- Global error interceptor sends errors to `react-toastify`

## Axios Configuration
Centralized in `QueryProvider.tsx`:
- `baseURL`, `Content-Type` header
- Auth header injection
- Global error interceptor → `react-toastify`

## Access Control
- Use `useAccessControls()` hook; never hard-code role checks in components
- Gate buttons/actions with permission checks:
```ts
if (canWrite('permission_code')) { 
  // render action
}
```

## Security Best Practices
- Tokens stored in `localStorage` key `_token`
- Expired/invalid tokens redirect to `/logout` (see interceptor)
- Never interpolate user input into URLs; pass via `params` or `query-string`
- All endpoints require accompanying Zod schema validation

## State Management
- Prefer `useState`/`useReducer` locally; avoid global state libraries
- Derive UI state from TanStack Query where possible
- TanStack Query is single source of server state; no bare Axios calls in components

